                            <comment id="491822" author="JIRAUSER19447" created="Wed, 25 Mar 2026 15:37:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I have been understanding/learning the concepts used in this ticket. I have read about IPv6 link-local addresses from the RFE. I was going through the code execution path of lnetctl using GDB. I found that lnet uses netlink sockets for configuring lnet interfaces. I also read about netlink interface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I am confused/stuck on what to do next. Is there any document or previous Jira that can help me here. Or any other guidance on how to proceed further.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491825" author="adilger" created="Wed, 25 Mar 2026 16:05:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I don&apos;t think this has anything to do with Netlink.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is a specific check it the socklnd configuration code that disallows link-local addresses, and the proposal here is to remove that check. I don&apos;t have it handy, but &quot;git grep &apos;link.*local&apos; lnet/&quot; or &quot;git log --grep &apos;link.*local&apos;&quot; should find it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
